<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of Queensland</h1><p class="st-meta">1859 CE – 1901 CE · capital Brisbane</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The northeastern Australian colony that grew from a penal station into a land of sugar, gold and cattle, and elected the world's first Labour government.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>A penal settlement for reoffending convicts was set up at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moreton-bay">Moreton Bay</a> in 1824 and moved to the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brisbane">Brisbane</a> in 1825. The district opened to free settlement in 1842 and was part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-new-south-wales">Colony of New South Wales</a> until 6 June 1859, when it became a separate colony with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-bowen">George Bowen</a> as governor and Brisbane as capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Pastoralists spread across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aboriginal-australians">Aboriginal</a> lands, with frontier violence carried out by settlers and the Native Police. Gold rushes at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gympie">Gympie</a>, Charters Towers and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-morgan-queensland">Mount Morgan</a> brought wealth. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">Sugar plantations</a> used some 62,000 Pacific Islanders, many recruited by deception in the trade known as blackbirding. The shearers' strike of 1891 helped found the Labour Party, and in 1899 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anderson-dawson">Anderson Dawson</a> briefly led the world's first Labour government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Queensland voted for federation in 1899 and became a state of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/commonwealth-of-australia">Commonwealth of Australia</a> in 1901. Most Pacific Islander labourers were deported under the new federation's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-australia-policy">White Australia policy</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/colony-of-queensland.jpg" alt="Colony of Queensland" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Fry1989 eh? · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Queensland_(1876%E2%80%931901).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1859 CE – 1901 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Brisbane</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>George Bowen, Samuel Griffith</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism, Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/australia">Australia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Queensland</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1880&amp;focus=colony-of-queensland" aria-label="Colony of Queensland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8700 3185 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Colony of Queensland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M9020 3441L8856 3661M9020 3441L4997 651M9020 3441L8774 3709"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8856 3661h0M4997 651h0M8774 3709h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M9020 3441h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M9020 3441h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Brisbane. <a href="/atlas?year=1880&amp;focus=colony-of-queensland">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
